\begin{abstract}
The rapid expansion of edge‑computing platforms has created a pressing need for energy‑efficient neural network inference. Existing quantization and compression techniques either compromise model accuracy or require extensive hardware support, limiting deployment on resource‑constrained devices. We introduce a mixed‑precision quantization framework that jointly optimizes layer‑wise bit‑widths and hardware‑aware scaling factors via a differentiable search. A lightweight reinforcement‑learning controller adapts precision settings to meet strict latency budgets while preserving model accuracy, representing a novel synergy between automated search and hardware‑aware optimization. Experiments on ImageNet and COCO demonstrate up to 3.2× reduction in inference energy with less than 1 % top‑1 accuracy loss compared to full‑precision baselines. The framework enables state‑of‑the‑art vision models to run on micro‑controllers, opening new opportunities for on‑device AI in real‑world applications.
\end{abstract}